# The Nodes list's filter chips: which of the roster is below the chip bar, as a control the
# reader can see and a press the frame names.
#
# Four things to watch, and the last is the one that would be a bug nobody could see.
#
#   - The filters are chips on one bar with the search and the sort - [Find] [All] [Direct]
#     [Pinned] ... [Sort] - and the chosen one is the filled chip. The set is on the panel, so
#     the list's state reads at a glance rather than off a word in a value column.
#   - Left and Right walk the chips and change nothing: the focus ring moves, and A is the press
#     that chooses. The shoulders still walk the tabs - that split is the whole reason the d-pad's
#     axis could be spent here, and it is the map's split one tab along.
#   - The heading's count is what is *drawn*, not what is held, and it is there only while the
#     reader has narrowed the list. "Nodes (n of m)" already means "there is more than this", so a
#     filter needs no sentence of its own; watch the first number move as the chips are chosen and
#     the second stay where it is.
#   - Under Direct, every row has a staircase against its trailing edge and none of them says
#     "hop" or "mqtt". That is the row asking mesh_ui_node_signal_heard() rather than a looser
#     question of its own - if it asked `hops_away == 0` instead, Delta Camp would be in this
#     list with nothing beside its name.

scene demo
scale 4
clock 2026-01-12 19:12
config

# One node the reader has chosen to keep, so the last chip has something to show.
pin ECHO

tab nodes
hold 1600

# The ring starts on All, the chip that is lit. Right moves it onto Direct and nothing else
# changes; A chooses it. The nodes heard with no relay in the way, which is the question the
# trailing staircase answers one row at a time and this answers for the whole list.
key right
hold 900
key a
hold 2200

# Pinned, the same two presses. The star in the marker gutter is the same fact this chip filters
# on, which is why the chip is called what X is called.
key right
hold 900
key a
hold 2200

# And back the way we came, which is the half a set stepped only by A never had: the walk runs
# both ways, so a reader who has gone one too far presses the other direction rather than
# wrapping the whole set.
key left
hold 900
key a
hold 2000

# The rows under it are still rows: the cursor walks off the bar into them, Left and Right go
# back to being the tab switch there, and A opens a node exactly as it does with no filter on.
# This is the half that is a picture of a bug if it is wrong - a filtered row that opened the
# roster's node rather than the row's would look right. The fifth row under Direct is Foxtrot
# Mobile; the fifth node of the whole roster is Delta Camp.
key down 5
hold 1200
key a
hold 1800
key b
hold 700
